{"name":"Blue Android Base","hex":"#5a79ba","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"android","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A robot that is designed to look and act like a human being (not necessarily a male one).","An artificial human."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Possessing human qualities.","Of the pelvis, having a narrow anterior segment and a heart-shaped brim, typically found in the male."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/android"},{"term":"base","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something from which other things extend; a foundation.\n A supporting, lower or bottom component of a structure or object.","A supporting, lower or bottom component of a structure or object."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To give as its foundation or starting point; to lay the foundation of.","To be located (at a particular place)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/base"}],"entries":[{"title":"Android (operating system)","blocks":[{"text":"Android is an operating system developed by Google, designed primarily for smartphones and tablets, based on a modified version of the Linux kernel and other open-source software. First released in 2008, Android is the world's most widely used operating system with 3.9 billion users, and the most used operating system for smartphones. The latest version, released on June 16, 2026, is Android 17."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Android_(operating_system)"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/HTC_Android_T-Mobile_G1.jpg/330px-HTC_Android_T-Mobile_G1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/HTC_Android_T-Mobile_G1.jpg/330px-HTC_Android_T-Mobile_G1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"HTC Dream or T-Mobile G1, the first commercially released device running Android (2008)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHTC_Android_T-Mobile_G1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/A_Press_Conference_for_the_Launch_of_Nexus_7_on_September_27%2C_2012_in_Seoul_from_acrofan_3.JPG/500px-A_Press_Conference_for_the_Launch_of_Nexus_7_on_September_27%2C_2012_in_Seoul_from_acrofan_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/A_Press_Conference_for_the_Launch_of_Nexus_7_on_September_27%2C_2012_in_Seoul_from_acrofan_3.JPG/500px-A_Press_Conference_for_the_Launch_of_Nexus_7_on_September_27